  "121": {
    "inputs": {
      "text": "[global prompt]\n\nA fixed industrial CCTV video based on the provided reference image. The entire video must remain a single, unchanged wide security-camera view from start to finish. The original full-frame composition, camera position, viewing angle, perspective, equipment layout, and lighting must remain exactly the same throughout the video.\n\n[camera]\n\nThe camera is a permanently mounted CCTV camera overlooking an industrial site. It must remain completely fixed, with no movement, shaking, panning, tilting, zooming, tracking, or reframing. The frame must remain unchanged throughout the entire video.\n\n[event start]\n\nAt the beginning of the video, the industrial site is still and operating normally. Shortly afterward, a small early-stage fire naturally ignites in one plausible ground-level area near equipment or stored materials.\n\n[fire details]\n\nThe fire must remain localized to a single location. The fire should stay small, but the orange flames must be clearly and distinctly visible within the original wide CCTV frame.\n\nThe flames should flicker naturally without suddenly growing larger or rising intensely. The fire must not spread widely to nearby equipment or materials and must not develop into a severe fire.\n\n[smoke details]\n\nA small amount of thin, light gray smoke is produced by the flames. The smoke should rise slowly above the fire source and remain light and low in density.\n\nThe smoke must not spread widely, become thick black smoke, or obscure nearby equipment or the background.\n\n[duration]\n\nThe small localized fire must continue until the end of the video. The flame size and smoke volume must not increase significantly over time. The fire must not explode or rapidly spread to the surrounding area.\n\n[motion constraint]\n\nOnly the small flames and the limited amount of smoke at the fire location are allowed to move. All other equipment, background elements, structures, and lighting must remain completely static. No people or vehicles may appear.\n\n\n",
      "clip": [
        "346",
        0
      ]
    },
    "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
    "_meta": {
